<title>FRANCE: Pinault-Printemps rises on mixed rumours.</title>
<headline>Pinault-Printemps rises on mixed rumours.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in retailer Pinault-Printemps-La Redoute rose on Friday with dealers mentioning a number of rumours.</p>
<p>The CDR consortium, which sells former Credit Lyonnais assets, declined to comment on market talk it was about to sell its 25 percent stake in Arthemis to Francois Pinault.</p>
<p>Arthemis is the holding company of Pinault-Printemps-La Redoute which is controlled by Pinault.</p>
<p>The shares in Pinault-Printemps were up 3.03 percent at 2,347 francs at 1534 GMT.</p>
<p>Other rumours in the market linked to the group were a possible share swap in a buy-out for minorities in its Rexel unit or the Paribas finance house Cetelem.</p>
<p>A spokeswoman for Pinault had no comment.</p>
</text>
